{
  "note": [
    "Cross-implementation vectors for email normalisation (spec 6.2).",
    "",
    "TypeScript normaliseEmail() in crypto/src/derive.ts feeds the Argon2id",
    "salt, so an address that normalises two ways derives two master keys and",
    "the member is locked out of their own vault. Python compares the same",
    "address against a tenant's ownerEmail to decide who may initialise it, so",
    "the two languages normalising differently refuses the legitimate owner.",
    "Neither failure is visible until it happens.",
    "",
    "Every string is written as a list of hex code points rather than as text.",
    "A file holding literal NFD characters would be silently recomposed by an",
    "editor, a git filter or a JSON tool, and the NFD cases below - the whole",
    "reason this file exists - would then pass without testing anything.",
    "",
    "Produced by running crypto/src/derive.ts, which is the authority: the",
    "browser is where a master key is actually derived. Do not regenerate",
    "these to match a changed implementation; a change here invalidates every",
    "existing account's salt."
  ],
